WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
Speaker 1: All right, the big foreign policy&nbsp;
news overnight is that Joe Biden is going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:11.520
leave Afghanistan on the schedule he most&nbsp;
recently put in place, which is August&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:18.320
31st. And I have to tell you, foreign policy is&nbsp;
very complicated. Foreign policy typically has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:24.400
ifs, ands and buts. But as many of you have&nbsp;
continued to email me about, some in agreement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:32.720
some in disagreement, this is one of the clearest&nbsp;
and most black white sort of decisive ways that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.960
I've seen foreign policy carried out. And I&nbsp;
agree with it 100 percent. And we're going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:42.240
talk about why. But the big news is that indeed,&nbsp;
Joe Biden is confirming that the United States&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:47.840
will keep its August 31st deadline, saying&nbsp;
yesterday, the sooner we finish, the better.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:53.600
Joe Biden said yesterday the U.S. is on track to&nbsp;
complete its hurried airlift in Afghanistan by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:58.960
August 31st. Acknowledging he does not plan to&nbsp;
keep American troops in the country any longer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:04.960
even as questions remain over who will be able&nbsp;
to leave and when. In late afternoon remarks at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:10.000
the White House, Biden recognized the success of&nbsp;
the mission will depend largely on cooperation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.480
from the Taliban. He said he's asked military&nbsp;
leaders to be ready with contingency options&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:20.640
to adjust the timetable if it becomes necessary.&nbsp;
We are currently on pace to finish by August 31,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:28.560
he said. I am determined to complete our&nbsp;
mission. This is completely the right decision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:36.480
now on cost alone, looking at what has been spent&nbsp;
in Afghanistan over the last 20 years, leaving is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:44.000
completely justified on failed policy alone,&nbsp;
meaning we aren't making any progress there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:51.360
And in fact, the longer we stay, we are merely&nbsp;
delaying the inevitable while spending more money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:57.680
on failed policy alone. You could justify leaving&nbsp;
on the length of time we've been there alone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:02.640
You could even maybe justify leaving, meaning even&nbsp;
if you could justify the cost, which you can't,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.800
even if you could make the case that you&nbsp;
were somehow succeeding, which we aren't.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:14.080
Just the fact that it's been 20 years would in&nbsp;
some sense justify leaving. But it's all of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:20.320
things and more. And we have to be able to look at&nbsp;
it and say Barack Obama was wrong to stay there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:27.200
Donald Trump was wrong to stay there. Joe Biden&nbsp;
is right to leave. That's the big picture. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:32.320
the rest of it is details. Now, they are important&nbsp;
details. The details are important for sure. Like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:38.160
for example, did we adequately plan for getting&nbsp;
people out? And that includes Americans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:44.960
but that also includes what is happening from the&nbsp;
standpoint of refugees. Did we plan appropriately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:52.720
for the humanitarian fallout and on and on. But&nbsp;
we have now evacuated more than 70000 people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:56.560
And here is Joe Biden explaining it.
Speaker 2: As of this afternoon, we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:01.040
helped evacuate seventy thousand seven hundred&nbsp;
people just since August of fourteen seventy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:10.560
five thousand nine hundred people since the end of&nbsp;
July, just in the past 12 hours, another 19 U.S.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:18.640
military flights, 18 C 17 and one C-130 carrying&nbsp;
approximately six thousand four hundred evacuees.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:24.640
And thirty one coalition flights carrying five&nbsp;
thousand six hundred people have left Kabul&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:32.800
just in the last 12 hours. A total of 50 more&nbsp;
flights, 12000 more people since we updated you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:37.680
this morning. These numbers are a testament to&nbsp;
the efforts of our brave service women and men&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:42.960
to our diplomats on the ground in Kabul&nbsp;
and to our allies still standing with us.&nbsp;

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:50.800
Speaker 1: And as I tweeted to much reaction&nbsp;
last night, Biden gets out of a 20 year quagmire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:58.560
in Afghanistan, evacuates more than 70000 people.&nbsp;
And as of now, no Americans have died. And we're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:07.040
supposed to believe that this is bad. And you've&nbsp;
seen Fox News say it's bad because, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:13.040
it's Biden. You've seen other media outlets&nbsp;
sometimes considered left, sometimes considered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:18.400
centrist, sometimes merely just corporate media&nbsp;
outlets play up. Well, shouldn't we maintain a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:24.160
presence? Shouldn't we stay, et cetera? No,&nbsp;
no. And this has really exposed the kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:31.760
corporatist pro it's not even really pro-war.&nbsp;
It's just pro foreign intervention, status quo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:36.240
or default position of so many of the media&nbsp;
outlets, even considered to be left by some.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:42.560
So now we get to the details and of course, the&nbsp;
details are important. Afghanistan fell to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:47.280
Taliban in a weekend. Now, there are some who&nbsp;
are looking at that and are saying, well, that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:52.240
evidence that we didn't handle the withdrawal&nbsp;
appropriately. I would actually say the opposite.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.880 --> 00:05:00.320
I would say that if after 20 years Afghanistan&nbsp;
fell to the Taliban in a weekend, there was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:06.320
nothing you could do to prevent that from&nbsp;
happening sooner or later if you left. And the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:11.360
fact that it happened in a weekend is proof that&nbsp;
we should be out of there. We should have left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:19.440
sooner, not stayed longer. So this is arguably the&nbsp;
best thing that Joe Biden has done. And you have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:25.280
to really look at the motivations of the different&nbsp;
people that are criticizing the decision. There&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:30.080
are some on the left who are criticizing the&nbsp;
decision merely because they want to show their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:33.840
progressive credentials and they want to criticize&nbsp;
Biden no matter what. That's some people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:38.800
Similarly, there are those on the right who are&nbsp;
ignoring the fact that Donald Trump had the exact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:42.320
same plan. It would have been carried out in&nbsp;
the exact same way, no matter what he tells you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:46.400
And they are saying, well, no, no, no, Biden did&nbsp;
it wrong. Trump would have done it correctly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:53.520
They are obviously incorrect about that as well.&nbsp;
And then, of course, you have the fact that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:59.360
so much of the media is saying, was this actually&nbsp;
right? Should we have stayed with Rababah?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:06.000
That confirms, as I mentioned, this kind of status&nbsp;
quo, pro intervention bias. The issues now are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:13.280
can we continue getting Americans out safely?&nbsp;
And how many Afghan lives can we also save? And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:18.800
that has to be a priority as well. But if we&nbsp;
look at everything Joe Biden has done so far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:26.000
this is one of the major accomplishments. This has&nbsp;
been a 20 year quagmire started by George W. Bush.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:34.000
We arguably never should have gone. If we did, we&nbsp;
should have left, what, 18, 17 years ago. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:39.920
that's in the most generous point, the most&nbsp;
generous interpretation. And we can't fall for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:45.520
the concern. Trolls, quite frankly, is what they&nbsp;
are on both sides. So if you want to email me and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:49.760
say, well, this could have been better planned or&nbsp;
that could have been better planned, sure, I'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:58.000
probably agree with you. But this was a decisive&nbsp;
action by Joe Biden. It was the right decisive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:05.600
action. And the idea that we should be criticizing&nbsp;
him for finally getting us out is really it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:12.000
it's depressing to see from how many different&nbsp;
sides. That's the perspective that we are seeing.

